  /dev/mapper/sys-nothere (/srv/nothere) of the old fstab is dropped: the device is not there
  /dev/sr0 (/media/cdrom0) of the old fstab is dropped: the device is not there
  /home is kept: the profile's users get their home directories and keys there; a home directory that is there already goes to the user of its name (its files change owner where the user's ID differs), its authorized_keys is replaced (the old one saved beside it)
  the source /opt/old/app of the bind mount at /srv/app was on the old root: the new system gets an empty directory there, so that the mount does not fail
  the source /srv/My\040Files of the bind mount at /mnt/my\040files was on the old root: the new system gets an empty directory there, so that the mount does not fail
  network file systems are kept as the old fstab has them; nfs-common or cifs-utils is installed for them on Ubuntu and Debian
  the logical volume /dev/mapper/sys-frozen is not active here (linear): what is on it is not seen
